# Database Configuration - HYBRID SETUP
# ======================================

# IMPORTANT: This system uses a HYBRID database architecture:
# Database file: system/Attendance.db (SQLite)
# - CREDENTIALS table: Always in SQLite (local)
# - FR_REGISTRATIONS table: PostgreSQL when database URL is set, otherwise SQLite

# PostgreSQL Database URLs (for FR_REGISTRATIONS table only)
# --------------------------------------------------------
# The system checks DEV_DATABASE_URL first, then falls back to DATABASE_URL

# Development Database (used locally)
# DEV_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://username:password@localhost:5432/registrations_dev

# Production Database (used on Replit)
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://username:password@hostname.region.aws.neon.tech/registrations

# How it works:
# - If DEV_DATABASE_URL is set: Uses development PostgreSQL
# - If only DATABASE_URL is set: Uses production PostgreSQL
# - If neither is set: Uses SQLite for everything

# When NO database URL is set:
# - All tables (CREDENTIALS, FR_REGISTRATIONS) use SQLite: system/Attendance.db

# When database URL IS set (DEV or PROD):
# - CREDENTIALS table: SQLite (system/Attendance.db) - local admin credentials
# - FR_REGISTRATIONS table: PostgreSQL - centralized registration registry

# Replit PostgreSQL Environment Variables
# ----------------------------------------
# When you create a PostgreSQL database on Replit, these are automatically set:
# - DATABASE_URL: Complete PostgreSQL connection string
# - PGHOST: Database hostname
# - PGUSER: Database username
# - PGPASSWORD: Database password
# - PGDATABASE: Database name

# Local Development
# -----------------
# Leave DATABASE_URL commented out.
# All tables will use SQLite (system/Attendance.db)

# Local Development
# -----------------
# Option 1: Use SQLite only (no setup needed)
#   - Leave both DEV_DATABASE_URL and DATABASE_URL commented out
#   - All tables use SQLite: system/Attendance.db

# Option 2: Use PostgreSQL for FR_REGISTRATIONS table
#   - Set DEV_DATABASE_URL to your local PostgreSQL instance
#   - CREDENTIALS stays in SQLite, FR_REGISTRATIONS goes to PostgreSQL

# Production Deployment (Replit)
# -------------------------------
# 1. Create PostgreSQL database via Replit Database tool (name: registrations)
# 2. DATABASE_URL will be automatically set in Replit environment
# 3. FR_REGISTRATIONS table will be created automatically on startup
# 4. CREDENTIALS table remains in local SQLite file

# Security Note
# -------------
# CREDENTIALS (admin logins) NEVER leave your local machine
# Only FR_REGISTRATIONS data is stored in the cloud
